        "node_id": "n_5_c23b71",
        "thought_text": "Consider using a different approach to efficiently find the pair of vectors with the minimal non-oriented angle. Instead of sorting all vectors and then checking adjacent pairs, use a sweep line algorithm or a bucket sort technique to group vectors into bins based on their polar angles. This allows for faster identification of potential pairs with small angular differences. Additionally, ensure that the algorithm handles edge cases, such as vectors very close to the boundary conditions of 0 and π, carefully to avoid numerical instability.",
